    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Young and Tanksley (1989a,b) suggested that selection using multiple markers (instead of single markers) can greatly accelerate the formation of NILs with very short introgressed segments. Likewise, selection for recurrent markers on nontarget chromosomes increases the rate of removal of donor DNA on other chromosomes.",
      "source_page": 426,
      "printed_page": 406,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter14:p034:b3"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        122.0,
        234.0,
